  "limits": [
    "SDK SIM only; no SGX hardware isolation, timing or performance result.",
    "Selected serial rollback-journal Unix-VFS route only; no WAL, mmap, concurrency or full POSIX/SQLite compatibility.",
    "The protected stop is trusted boundary-service enforcement at encbound_bridge_string, not a later SQLite object check.",
    "Only PROTECTED targets are rejected; raw pointers to COMPAT read-only application data are admitted by design.",
    "A normal host TMPDIR/SQLITE_TMPDIR value is a raw host pointer and is also rejected by the protected bridge; the benign control leaves both unset.",
    "The host knows the enclave base/canary offset; no ASLR or address-secrecy claim.",
    "The BASELINE Enclave_t.c retains the selected propagate_errno extension; Enclave_t.h and the untrusted bridge files match stock.",
    "In protected profiles the first hostile use aborts, so later azDirs reuse is only observable in BASELINE."
  ],
